  "summary": "To determine the crystalline versus amorphous content of your PEEK implant material, Differential Scanning Calorimetry (DSC) using EQ18 is the primary technique to calculate percent crystallinity from melting enthalpies. EQ17 (TGA) can provide supplementary information regarding thermal stability, while techniques like X-ray Diffraction (XRD), which is not currently available on the equipment list, would offer a direct structural measurement of crystallinity."
